      "text": "The driver's own device trace measures this trip at 4.58 km against an optimal route of 4.4 km — an excess of just 0.18 km, or 4.09% (ev-gps-00525.derived.deviation). POL-RD-01 requires the excess to exceed 0.8 km AND exceed 20% of the optimal distance; both tests must pass, and this trace fails both by a wide margin. No route deviation is established on this trip's own evidence. The rounded 4.5% deviation_pct carried on the trip record is not the governing figure — POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern, and the trace figure is 4.09%.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00525", "EV-TRIP-00525"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-08 places the initial burden on the rider: she must show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, measured from an unimpaired trace. The trace here is unimpaired — 85 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s, admissibility weight 1.0 — and it shows an excess of 0.18 km / 4.09%, below both POL-RD-01 gates. The burden therefore never shifts to the driver, and the deviation claim is not sustained.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00525"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-01 is explicit that where either establishment test fails, no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The rider's grievance — that the driver 'entered the wrong amount' — is a fare-keying complaint dressed up as a route deviation. On the question actually put by this dispute the trace answers in the driver's favour, and the route-deviation limb of the case is NO_ACTION.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00525", "EV-TRIP-00525"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip: fare_breakdown.fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE and the quoted fare was SGD 13.00. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, POL-RD-02 does not run, and no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however large the excess. The rider is already whole on distance and time, and the excess here is only 4.09% in any event.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00525"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider contests the full SGD 17.50, and nothing in the policy supports that. On an upfront-quoted fare the platform's own fare model publishes the only figure the record could yield — the SGD 4.50 difference between the 13.00 quoted and the 17.50 charged (pol_rd_11_remedy) — and no clause supports a FULL_REFUND here. The driver's statement on file explains the discrepancy candidly as a back-to-back booking keyed against the wrong passenger, a clerical slip, not a route choice and not any conduct the policy penalises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00525", "EV-TRIP-00525"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.pol_rd_11_remedy",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-09's billing-integrity route is empty on this record. The fare carries no ERP gantry lines (erp_gantries is empty, tolls_erp 0.00), no airport surcharge (airport_surcharge 0.00), and the trip does not originate at an airport — pickup is Bedok Mall, not Changi or Seletar. There is no unmatched gantry or wrongly applied surcharge for POL-RD-09(4) to bite on, so no billing-integrity finding can be recorded against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00525", "EV-TRIP-00525"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver shows zero deviation flags in the last 90 days against 250 completed trips — a ratio of 0.00, below both the 3-flag limb and the 0.05-with-40-trips limb of POL-RD-06. No repeat-deviation pattern is established, so neither the FULL_REFUND uplift nor the driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) is available. The rider's request for anything beyond a minor correction therefore has no footing in the policy.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00525"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's assertion that this is 'the fourth time in a year' comes with no evidence ID for any of the three alleged earlier incidents; POL-RD-08 provides that an assertion citing no evidence ID carries no weight and is discarded. Her own profile records no substantiated route-deviation claim in the last 60 days, and POL-GEN-01 forbids any adverse finding built on profile history rather than this trip's own evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00525"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

