    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the money moves, but only the amount that was charged above the quoted price. The fare you paid was SGD 17.50 (EV-FARE-00525, charged_total) against the SGD 13.00 quoted at booking (EV-FARE-00525, quoted_fare_sgd). This was an upfront-quoted trip (EV-FARE-00525, fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE), so the distance and time charges were fixed when the ride was booked and POL-RD-11 governs; POL-RD-02 does not run. POL-RD-11(a) refunds in full whatever was charged above that fixed quote plus the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09. Nothing is properly chargeable here: the ERP lines are 0.00, the trip ran from Bedok Mall to Parkway Parade and so neither originated nor ended at an airport, so no airport surcharge applies, and the waiting-time fee was 0.00 (properly_chargeable.total 0.00). The whole differential is therefore returned: 17.50 less 13.00 less 0.00 = SGD 4.50, which is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and already lands on a 0.05 boundary. The driver's statement that he keyed the other passenger's amount by mistake explains how the figure arose and is consistent with the ledger; it does not defeat the refund, because the rider agreed to SGD 13.00 and the extra SGD 4.50 was not the price of this drive. On the route-deviation limb the driver is correct: the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00525) measures 4.58 km against an optimal 4.4 km, an excess of 0.18 km / 4.09%, and POL-RD-01 requires an excess both above 0.8 km and above 20%. Both gates fail, so no deviation exists and no distance refund arises; the trace is unimpaired (85 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps), so the rider's burden under POL-RD-08 is not met on the road and never shifts to the driver. So the driver's claim of NO_ACTION is right about the route and wrong about the fare. No repeat-deviation pattern is established: the driver profile shows 0 deviation flags in 90 days against 250 completed trips, below both limbs of POL-RD-06, so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral. The rider's assertion that this is the fourth such incident in a year cites no evidence ID for the earlier occasions and carries no weight under POL-RD-08; profile history is context only under POL-GEN-01. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00525-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) is not relied on by either party and does not affect this ruling. The deciding figure is carried by EV-FARE-00525 at weight 1.0, so no discount applies."
  },
