    "explanation": "Rider and driver — this dispute is partly upheld, and it is upheld as a fare correction, not as a route-deviation refund.\n\nRoute. No deviation is established. The driver's own device trace (EV-GPS-00525: 85 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s) measures the drive at 4.58 km against an optimal route of 4.4 km — an excess of 0.18 km, or 4.09%. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to exceed 0.8 km AND exceed 20% of the optimal distance; both gates fail, so no deviation exists on this trip's own evidence and the route limb of the claim is not sustained. The 4.5% carried on the trip record is the rounded convenience copy; POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure (4.09%) govern.\n\nFare. This was an upfront-quoted trip: EV-FARE-00525 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with a quoted fare of SGD 13.00, while SGD 17.50 was taken. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, so the drive is not re-priced and POL-RD-02 does not run — but the amount by which the charge exceeded the quote is refunded in full. The same ledger shows no ERP gantry lines, no airport surcharge (the trip runs Bedok Mall to Parkway Parade, neither an airport, so none is chargeable) and no waiting-time fee, leaving properly chargeable lines of SGD 0.00 to set against the difference. SGD 17.50 charged − SGD 13.00 quoted − SGD 0.00 properly chargeable = SGD 4.50, which is also the platform's own published figure (pol_rd_11_remedy, available true) and sits above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor. The driver's filed statement — that he 'keyed in the other passenger's amount by mistake' — is an admission that the sum taken was not the price quoted, and it supports the correction; the figure itself, however, is read from the fare ledger.\n\nWhat is not owed, and why. The rider asked for the full SGD 17.50; that is not supported, because on an upfront-quoted fare the rider is already whole on distance and time and only the excess over the quote returns — SGD 4.50, not SGD 17.50. The driver's submission that nothing at all is due is likewise not accepted, because the SGD 4.50 above the quote was never consideration for this drive.\n\nReferrals and profile points. No repeat-deviation pattern arises: POL-RD-06 only runs on a material deviation, and the route here was clean; in any event the driver shows zero deviation flags in 90 days against 250 completed trips, so no conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) is produced. The billing-integrity route under POL-RD-09(4) is empty — no unmatched gantry and no misplaced surcharge — so no billing referral is recorded either. The rider's assertion that this is 'the fourth time in a year' cites no evidence ID for any earlier incident and carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and POL-GEN-01 forbids any adverse finding from profile history rather than this trip's evidence.\n\nConfidence. The ruling rests on EV-FARE-00525, admissibility status COMPLETE at weight 1.0, which carries the deciding figure; the bundle is clean and the driver's own statement corroborates. Confidence is set at 0.90, within the cap set by that weight and above the 0.70 escalation floor, so the case is decided and no escalation is engaged."
